From: xcentaurix
Subject: [PATCH] PlatformDisplaySurfaceless: join and register with Nexus before the first EGL call

Symptom (VU+ Ultimo 4K, Nexus/V3D GLES2 driver): the WebProcess dies with a SIGSEGV about 1 ms after the first HTTP response, right after the
Nexus join/register lines, reported as "WEB PROCESS TERMINATED (reason 0)". Found with gdb (a hardware watchpoint on mimalloc's main theap):

  crash:  mi_arenas_page_regular_alloc <- mi_page_fresh_alloc <- mi_page_queue_find_free_ex <- _mi_malloc_generic <- mi_malloc <- fastMalloc
          <- JSC::VM::create <- WebCore::mainThreadNormalWorldSingleton (InjectedBundleScriptWorld::normalWorldSingleton)
  cause:  theap_main.tld (the first word of mimalloc's static main-thread heap, initially &tld_main) holds 0x3008 = EGL_BAD_DISPLAY.
  writer: libEGL.so.1 (libv3ddriver.so), on the main thread, called from
          WebProcess::initializeWebProcess -> platformInitializeWebProcess -> initializePlatformDisplayIfNeeded -> PlatformDisplaySurfaceless::create

PlatformDisplaySurfaceless::create() starts with eglQueryString(EGL_NO_DISPLAY, EGL_EXTENSIONS). The driver rejects the display (it only knows handle 1)
with EGL_BAD_DISPLAY and stores the error in its per-thread state, which it fetches through pthread_getspecific(key) - and uses whatever non-NULL
value comes back without further checks (libv3ddriver.so 0x247e4). The key is only created by the Nexus join/register, which ran later (from
PlatformDisplayLibWPE/Default::create, patch 0017). Until then the key is 0, and pthread_getspecific(0) returns the value mimalloc registered under
its own key 0 (&theap_main). So the driver writes the error code into mimalloc's heap, and the next big allocation dereferences the garbage "tld".

Fix: call ensureNexusPlatformJoined() (patch 0017) at the top of PlatformDisplaySurfaceless::create() too, and unregister in the destructor, so no
EGL call precedes the join on any path. No-op on boxes without the Nexus libraries.

---
diff --git a/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/egl/PlatformDisplaySurfaceless.cpp b/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/egl/PlatformDisplaySurfaceless.cpp
index f7ad5f6..8229d81 100644
--- a/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/egl/PlatformDisplaySurfaceless.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/egl/PlatformDisplaySurfaceless.cpp
@@ -29,10 +29,24 @@
 #include "GLContext.h"
 #include <epoxy/egl.h>
 
+#if PLATFORM(WPE)
+#include "NexusEGLPlatformQuirk.h"
+#endif
+
 namespace WebCore {
 
 std::unique_ptr<PlatformDisplaySurfaceless> PlatformDisplaySurfaceless::create()
 {
+#if PLATFORM(WPE)
+    // This is the FIRST EGL call of a WebProcess that gets its display through WebProcess::initializePlatformDisplayIfNeeded()
+    // (m_rendererBufferTransportMode not empty), and eglQueryString(EGL_NO_DISPLAY, ...) below is rejected with EGL_BAD_DISPLAY. On a
+    // Nexus based Broadcom box (VU+ Ultimo 4K confirmed) the vendor libEGL keeps its per-thread state under a pthread key that only the
+    // Nexus join/register creates: before it, the key is still 0 and pthread_getspecific(0) returns mimalloc's slot (theap_main), so the
+    // driver stores 0x3008 into the first word of mimalloc's main heap. The next big allocation (JSC::VM::create) then dies in
+    // mi_arenas_page_regular_alloc. Join and register first, as PlatformDisplayLibWPE/Default already do.
+    ensureNexusPlatformJoined();
+#endif
+
     const char* extensions = eglQueryString(nullptr, EGL_EXTENSIONS);
     if (!GLContext::isExtensionSupported(extensions, "EGL_MESA_platform_surfaceless"))
         return nullptr;
@@ -60,6 +74,11 @@ PlatformDisplaySurfaceless::PlatformDisplaySurfaceless(Ref<GLDisplay>&& glDispla
 #endif
 }
 
-PlatformDisplaySurfaceless::~PlatformDisplaySurfaceless() = default;
+PlatformDisplaySurfaceless::~PlatformDisplaySurfaceless()
+{
+#if PLATFORM(WPE)
+    unregisterNexusPlatformIfJoined();
+#endif
+}
 
 } // namespace WebCore
